  "caption": "Quinn reached level 99 in a single all-nighter. The next morning, the thumb had other ideas.\n\nHours of texting, swiping and gaming can give tendons more work than they're ready for. It's usually a load issue rather than damage.\n\nWhat can help: cut back your biggest thumb habit for a couple of weeks, let voice-to-text handle long messages, take a break every 20–30 minutes, prop your device and support your forearms, and build grip and thumb strength with light resistance.\n\nPain that lasts beyond a few weeks, numbness or tingling, fingers that click or lock, or grip that's getting weaker is worth getting checked.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
